---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import AuditClose from "../components/AuditClose.astro";
---

<Site
  page="about"
  title="About Anchorline | Conviction, Intelligence & Execution"
  description="Anchorline Systems LLC is led by founder and CEO Kris McFadden. Learn about the convictions and operating principles behind the Anchorline Growth Engine."
  schemaType="AboutPage"
>
  <section class="container r-about-hero r-split">
    <figure class="founder-portrait">
      <img
        src="/kris-mcfadden.webp"
        alt="Kris McFadden, founder and CEO of Anchorline Systems"
        width="600"
        height="601"
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
      /><figcaption>
        <strong>Kris McFadden</strong><span
          >FOUNDER & CEO · ANCHORLINE SYSTEMS</span
        >
      </figcaption>
    </figure><div class="r-editorial">
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT ANCHORLINE</p><h1>
        Built by an operator, for organizations that want more.
      </h1><p class="r-lede">
        Good organizations need more than another idea or another tool. They
        need the judgment to see what matters—and the ability to turn that
        judgment into work that moves the organization forward.
      </p><p>
        Kris McFadden, MBA, leads Anchorline’s direction and operating
        standards. His MBA in Healthcare Management complements experience in
        organizational leadership, systems thinking, growth, and hands-on
        execution.
      </p><div class="r-actions"><CTA location="about-hero" /></div>
      <div class="founder-links" aria-label="Kris McFadden public profiles">
        <a
          href="https://krismcfadden.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >KrisMcFadden.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        ><a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/krismcfadden/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      "@id": "https://anchorlineai.com/about/#kris-mcfadden",
      name: "Kris McFadden",
      jobTitle: "Founder and CEO",
      honorificSuffix: "MBA",
      hasCredential: {
        "@type": "EducationalOccupationalCredential",
        credentialCategory: "degree",
        name: "MBA in Healthcare Management",
      },
      sameAs: [
        "https://krismcfadden.com",
        "https://www.linkedin.com/in/krismcfadden/",
      ],
      worksFor: {
        "@id": "https://anchorlineai.com/#organization",
      },
      url: "https://anchorlineai.com/about/",
      image: "https://anchorlineai.com/kris-mcfadden.webp",
    }).replace(/</g, "\\u003c")}
  />
  <section class="r-section container r-split">
    <div class="r-editorial">
      <p class="eyebrow">LEADERSHIP THAT STAYS CLOSE TO THE WORK</p><h2>
        Strategy should survive<br />contact with reality.
      </h2>
    </div><div class="editorial-copy">
      <p class="large-copy">
        A clear point of accountability. From the first question to the next
        decision.
      </p><p>
        Anchorline exists to help established businesses and organizations
        increase visibility, create real opportunities, and turn more of them
        into measurable results. We connect the strategy with the practical work
        required to deliver it.
      </p><p>
        The Growth Engine is one expression of that thinking: a flagship
        commercial system that connects intelligence, acquisition, conversion,
        and follow-up rather than treating them as separate projects.
      </p><p>
        Anchorline also creates practical insight, content, and educational
        media when those assets help people understand a problem and make a
        better decision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container">
    <p class="eyebrow">OPERATING PRINCIPLES</p><h2>
      How we approach the work.
    </h2><div class="principles-ledger">
      <article>
        <span class="mono">01</span><h3>Inspect before acting.</h3><p>
          Understand the business, existing infrastructure, and intended
          conversion before recommending a change.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span class="mono">02</span><h3>Connect the system.</h3><p>
          Choose capabilities for their contribution to the acquisition motion,
          not as isolated line items.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span class="mono">03</span><h3>Make responsibility clear.</h3><p>
          Define scope, ownership, review, and the next action. AI capability
          does not replace human judgment.
        </p>
      </article><article>
        <span class="mono">04</span><h3>Show the evidence.</h3><p>
          Separate observations from assumptions and illustrative work from
          verified client outcomes.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section foundation-section" id="foundation">
    <div class="container foundation-composition">
      <p class="eyebrow">OUR FOUNDATION</p><div>
        <blockquote>
          “Because He is, we are—and everything we build reflects that reality.”
        </blockquote><p>
          Anchorline’s convictions shape how we serve, lead, and build.
          Technology, rightly ordered, should support purposeful work,
          responsible stewardship, and operational excellence.
        </p><p>
          That foundation is expressed through accountable decisions, honest
          claims, and care for the people and organizations our work affects.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container r-framework-note">
    <p>
      Anchorline uses its proprietary 2ndBrainOS operating framework to connect
      research, knowledge, automation and execution behind the work.
    </p><a href="/approach/" class="text-link"
      >How we work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    >
  </div>
  <AuditClose />
</Site>
